# 51. COMMON BUFFER OVERFLOW TYPES

## Stack-based overflow

Occurs in stack memory.

## Heap-based overflow

Occurs in dynamically allocated heap memory.

## Integer overflow

Arithmetic wraps around and may lead to unsafe size calculations.

## Format-string vulnerability

Improper use of formatted output functions can expose or modify memory.

## Use-after-free

Program accesses memory after it has been released.

These are different memory-safety vulnerabilities.

---

# 52. STACK VS HEAP

| Stack | Heap |
|---|---|
| Function-related data | Dynamic memory |
| Local variables | Runtime allocations |
| Function call state | Objects/buffers |
| Often structured around stack frames | Dynamically managed |
| Stack overflow can corrupt stack data | Heap corruption affects allocator/object data |

