# 53. FORMAT STRING

Unsafe pattern:

```c
printf(user_input);
```

Safer:

```c
printf("%s", user_input);
```

Why?

The first version may interpret attacker-controlled characters as formatting directives.

Again:

> This is a different vulnerability from a classic buffer overflow.

