# 67. COMMON MISTAKES

### Mistake 1

> "It crashed, therefore RCE."

Wrong.

### Mistake 2

> "Buffer overflow means EIP/RIP is controllable."

Not necessarily.

### Mistake 3

> "ASLR means the vulnerability isn't real."

Wrong.

### Mistake 4

> "DEP prevents buffer overflows."

Wrong.

DEP limits code execution from certain memory regions; it does not prevent the underlying memory corruption.

### Mistake 5

> "One crash proves exploitability."

Wrong.

