# 76. DAY 39 QUICK REVISION

### Buffer Overflow

> Data exceeds the allocated buffer and may corrupt adjacent memory.

### Exploit

> Technique that takes advantage of a vulnerability.

### Payload

> Code/action delivered after exploitation.

### Offset

> Distance from input start to relevant overwritten control data.

### EIP

> x86 instruction pointer.

### RIP

> x86-64 instruction pointer.

### ASLR

> Randomizes memory addresses.

### DEP/NX

> Helps prevent execution from non-executable memory.

### Canary

> Detects certain stack corruption.

### CFG

> Restricts certain indirect control-flow transfers.

### NOP

> No Operation.

### Shellcode

> Machine-code payload concept.

